    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d129">

                <pb facs="0158" n="146" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg146"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">842.20 Defense/2: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-08-22T11:00:00-03:00">August 22, 1940—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>417. For the Under Secretary. President Vargas and Aranha<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d129-f1"/> are both harrying me with questions about our recent
                    negotiations with Canada. Is there anything that you can let me have for them on
                    this?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d129-f1" n="5" xml:id="d129-f1-content">
                <p>Oswaldo Aranha, Brazilian Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
